  "coverage": "complete",
  "notes": [
    "Complete list: 8 actions (osc.js updateActions, line 150) and 9 feedbacks (osc.js updateFeedbacks, line 669: 8 boolean, 1 value). Nothing is generated at runtime.",
    "Connection config (not part of the schema, osc.js getConfigFields): host, targetPort (default 8000, 1-65535), protocol (udp default, tcp, tcp-raw), listen (Listen for Feedback, default false) and feedbackPort (UDP only). The feedbacks only work with listen enabled.",
    "Not catalogued: static-text option 'warning' (id warning) in send_boolean, send_blob and osc_feedback_bool. Four textinputs set minLength: 1 (osc.js:109 is a config field; path fields of osc_feedback_midi, osc_feedback_multi_specific, osc_feedback_value), which the schema cannot hold; they are mentioned in the option description.",
    "Numeric fields: send_int and osc_feedback_int use asInteger over the 32-bit range; send_float and osc_feedback_float use +-3.4028235e38 without step or asInteger. The option values of osc_feedback_int/float are compared with parseFloat of the received first argument.",
    "send_multiple argument parsing (osc.js:280): when the text parses as a JSON array it is mapped element by element (integers become i, other numbers f, strings s, true/false T/F, other element types are dropped); otherwise a tokenizer is used: numbers without a point are i, with a point f, 'true'/'false' are T/F, quoted text (double or single quotes, typographic double quotes are normalized) is s, everything else is s.",
    "osc_feedback_multi parses its Arguments text with a different routine (helpers.js parseArguments: split on spaces, numbers without a point parseInt, with a point parseFloat, quotes stripped, no true/false handling), so booleans are not matched by it. Comparison is strict equality per argument.",
    "osc_feedback_noargs returns true once per received message and then deletes the stored message (a debounce, osc.js:1251). The _specific feedback compares argument [index]: the numeric comparisons require both sides to be finite numbers, the '... as String' variants compare text (booleans as 'true'/'false').",
    "send_blob: base64 (default) or hex, spaces and commas are removed before decoding. send_midi / osc_feedback_midi use the 4-byte OSC MIDI argument [portId, status, data1, data2]; program and channelpressure send data2 = 0; pitch bend is sent as value + 8192 split into LSB/MSB.",
    "The module also provides variables (latest_received_*, latest_sent_*) in osc.js:1315, not catalogued.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base 2.1.3: options support expressions, except fields with disableAutoExpression."
  ],
